TOPIC 1 — WHAT IS A STRING?  (“ “)
A string is a sequence of characters enclosed within quotation marks.
A string can contain:

Alphabets
Digits
Special characters
Symbols
Spaces


Examples
"Python"
'Computer Science'
"12345"
"Python123"
"Hello@123"
""
Example
name = "Python"
Here:
name     → variable
"Python" → string
Checking the data type
