TOPIC 6 — STRING INDEXING
Indexing means accessing individual characters of a string using their position.
Consider:
s = "PYTHON"
Positive indexing
Character :  P   Y   T   H   O   N
Index     :  0   1   2   3   4   5
Therefore:
print(s[0])
Output:
P
print(s[3])
Output:
H

TOPIC 7 — NEGATIVE INDEXING
Python also allows indexing from the right side.
Character :   P    Y    T    H    O    N
Positive  :   0    1    2    3    4    5
Negative  :  -6   -5   -4   -3   -2   -1
Therefore:
print(s[-1])
Output:
N
print(s[-2])
Output:
O
Important rule
First character → s[0]
Last character  → s[-1]

TOPIC 8 — INDEX OUT OF RANGE
Consider:
s = "Python"
Valid indexes:
0 1 2 3 4 5
This is invalid:
print(s[6])
It produces:
IndexError 
Remember
For a string of length n:
Positive indexes → 0 to n-1
Negative indexes → -n to -1

TOPIC 9 — STRINGS ARE IMMUTABLE
Immutable means that an existing string cannot be changed character by character.
Example:
