Consider:
s[-1:-7:-2]
The indexes visited are:
-1 → -3 → -5
The characters at those positions are then selected.
Important rule
When the step is negative:
Movement is from right to left.

TOPIC 19 — HOW TO SOLVE COMPLEX SLICING QUESTIONS
For every complex slice:
s[start:stop:step]
follow these steps:
Step 1
Identify the starting index.
Step 2
Identify the stopping boundary.
Step 3
Identify the step.
Step 4
Determine the direction.
Step 5
Write the indexes actually visited.
Step 6
Convert indexes into characters.

